---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Beyond the Headlines – Privacy policy"
  exactTitle="Beyond the Headlines – Privacy policy"
  path="/beyondtheheadlines/privacy/"
  description="Privacy policy for Beyond the Headlines, a free Claude plugin that writes a weekly AI news brief. The plugin runs in your own Claude account, and its author receives and stores none of your data."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Beyond the Headlines</p>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="post-meta" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Last updated 31 October 2026</p>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      Beyond the Headlines runs inside your own Claude account. It has no
      servers, code, scripts, tracking or analytics of its own. I don't
      receive, see or store your profile, your briefs, your conversations,
      your emails or anything else you do with it.
    </p>

    <h2>Who I am</h2>
    <p>
      Beyond the Headlines is a free, open-source (MIT) Claude plugin by
      Laurence Timms, an individual developer in the UK. The source is on <a href="https://github.com/laurencetimms/plugins">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      It contains one skill, the AI News Analyst. It writes a weekly brief on
      what AI is doing to work, power, knowledge and people.
    </p>

    <h2>What the plugin is</h2>
    <p>
      The plugin is a set of written instructions (skills). Claude follows
      them in your account. There is no software of mine running anywhere
      else.
    </p>

    <h2>What data is involved, and where it lives</h2>
    <p>All of it stays in your own accounts.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Your interest profile.</strong> This is a document you write
        and own. It holds only what you tell the analyst for this purpose: why
        you follow AI, what you already know, the lenses and stories you
        choose, what you want less of, your delivery preferences, and a log of
        each brief's menu and the items you picked. You choose where it is
        stored during setup: a Claude Doc, a Google Doc, a Notion page, or a
        file in your project. It isn't built from your chat history or
        Claude's memory, and the analyst adds no conclusions of its own about
        you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your briefs.</strong> You choose how they arrive: by email to
        your own address through your own Gmail connection, as a document in
        your own storage, or as a chat reply. They are never sent to anyone
        else.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A scheduled task.</strong> If you choose email or document
        delivery and your account supports it, setup creates one weekly
        scheduled task in your Claude account. You can pause, change or delete
        it at any time.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Web research.</strong> Claude searches the web and reads
        public pages to write each brief. No personal data is put into the
        searches.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Third parties</h2>
    <p>
      Everything runs on Claude, which is provided by Anthropic under <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy">Anthropic's privacy policy</a>.
      If you store your profile or emails in Google or Notion, those
      companies handle them under their own privacy policies. I have no
      access to any of it.
    </p>

    <h2>Usage figures from the directory</h2>
    <!-- Laurence: confirm against the directory portal's Usage tab before publishing. -->
    <p>
      If the plugin is listed in Anthropic's directory, Anthropic shows me
      usage figures for it. These include things like the number of installs,
      which versions are in use, how often the skill runs, and error rates.
      They don't include the content of anyone's profile, briefs or
      conversations.
    </p>

    <h2>Keeping and deleting your data</h2>
    <p>I keep nothing. You control everything.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Delete the profile document to remove your profile.</li>
      <li>Delete the scheduled task to stop the briefs.</li>
      <li>Uninstall the plugin to remove it.</li>
      <li>Emails stay in your inbox until you delete them.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      For data held by Anthropic, Google or Notion, make your request to
      those companies.
    </p>

    <h2>This web page</h2>
    <p>
      This page sets no cookies and runs no analytics or tracking. Its fonts
      are loaded from Google Fonts, so Google receives your IP address and
      browser details when you open it. The site is hosted on Cloudflare,
      which handles the request in the ordinary way for any website.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The plugin isn't intended for anyone under 18.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, I'll post the new version on this page with a
      new "last updated" date. Significant changes to what the plugin does
      will also be noted in the plugin's README on <a href="https://github.com/laurencetimms/plugins">GitHub</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy? <a href="/coaching/#contact">Get in touch</a> through the contact form on this site.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
